    self_error_used_where_error_fatal_intended_family_2026-08-08, 1, "2026-11-07 narrow GPU dispatch source repair landed PR7652 merge0b1339155ab53d1599c7d3ea8018ce28f3cfc425, reviewed head84e362e460b; verification waiting, owner compiler MIR. Only gpu_global_id/gpu_local_id/gpu_block_id/gpu_block_dim/gpu_grid_dim perform dimension validation; nonconstant dimensions are fatal and evaluated once for recovery. Nonliteral atomic/data arguments retain ordinary once-only evaluation and source order. Future admitted-runtime command: \"$SIMPLE_BIN\" test test/01_unit/compiler/mir/gpu_dimension_fatal_spec.spl --mode=interpreter. Real MIR owner assertions are authored; runtime/compiler/core/MCP/native/docgen NOT_RUN. Evidence doc/08_tracking/bug/self_error_used_where_error_fatal_intended_family_2026-08-08.md and mirrored gpu_dimension_fatal_spec manual. This narrow source fix does not close the wider diagnostic family; canonical Open status and prior cycle history remain unchanged."
    self_error_used_where_error_fatal_intended_family_2026-08-08, 0, "asm_and_targets.spl present with error()/error_fatal() pair; the prefix allowlist in driver_pipeline_lowering.spl leaves the enum-lookup-mis"

